-> 0.97.0 (⚠ API breaking changes)\n\n### ⚠ `onepipeline` breaking changes\n\n```text\n--- failure constructible_struct_adds_field: struct exhaustively constructible through public API adds field ---\n\nDescription:\nA pub struct that could be exhaustively constructed with a literal using only public API has a new pub field, breaking existing exhaustive literals.\n        ref: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/struct-expr.html\n       impl: https://github.com/obi1kenobi/cargo-semver-checks/tree/v0.51.0/src/lints/constructible_struct_adds_field.ron\n\nFailed in:\n  field TaskRecord.priority in /tmp/.tmpOsgDeb/onepipeline/src/plan.rs:1606\n\n--- failure enum_struct_variant_field_added: pub enum struct variant field added ---\n\nDescription:\nAn enum's exhaustive struct variant has a new field, which has to be included when constructing or matching on this variant.\n        ref: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/attributes/type_system.html#the-non_exhaustive-attribute\n       impl: https://github.com/obi1kenobi/cargo-semver-checks/tree/v0.51.0/src/lints/enum_struct_variant_field_added.ron\n\nFailed in:\n  field phase of variant HumanItemsCommand::Raise in /tmp/.tmpOsgDeb/onepipeline/src/human_items.rs:551\n  field context of variant HumanItemsCommand::Raise in /tmp/.tmpOsgDeb/onepipeline/src/human_items.rs:554\n\n--- failure enum_variant_added: enum variant added on exhaustive enum ---\n\nDescription:\nA publicly-visible enum without #[non_exhaustive] has a new variant.\n        ref: https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html#enum-variant-new\n       impl: https://github.com/obi1kenobi/cargo-semver-checks/tree/v0.51.0/src/lints/enum_variant_added.ron\n\nFailed in:\n  variant HumanItemsCommand:Config in /tmp/.tmpOsgDeb/onepipeline/src/human_items.rs:591\n  variant HumanItemsCommand:Watch in /tmp/.tmpOsgDeb/onepipeline/src/human_items.rs:598\n```\n\n<details><summary><i><b>Changelog</b></i></summary><p>\n\n<blockquote>\n\n##\n[0.97.0](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/compare/v0.96.2...v0.97.0)\n- 2026-10-31\n\n### Added\n\n- operate durable human items across host sessions\n([#1317](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1317))\n</blockquote>\n\n\n</p></details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with\n[release-plz](https://github.com/release-plz/release-plz/).","verified_at":"2026-10-31T04:07:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commit/99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a/comments","author":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e357c4f0d172762219fa9024417725d0663c53c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/e357c4f0d172762219fa9024417725d0663c53c1","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commit/e357c4f0d172762219fa9024417725d0663c53c1"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":3,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":3,"commits":[{"sha":"0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d","node_id":"C_kwDOTx8aUdoAKDAxNzNlNjI0OTg4MzFkMjc3MDExM2QwYzlhOTgxNDNkNDE2ZTEzNGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick DeRobertis","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-31T05:02:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-31T05:02:08Z"},"message":"perf: cut the onepipeline gate's work outside the e2e tier (#1320)\n\n## What\n\nSpeed up the non-e2e gate by reusing the debug build, compiling the\nstop-verdict release binary alongside other tasks, and running\nstaged-artifact corruption checks four at a time with faster fixture\ncompression. Preserve every existing test and assertion, with regression\ncoverage for build reuse, scheduling, artifact consumption, and build\nfailures.\n\n## Why\n\nBring pull-request test jobs toward the 30-minute goal and make local\ngates faster without cutting coverage. Linux’s non-e2e work alone\npreviously took 49.5 minutes, so skipping unaffected e2e suites cannot\nmeet that goal.\n\n## Additional info\n\nComparable-load host measurements show median pre-e2e gate time falling\nfrom 8,090 s to 4,580 s (43%). Total non-e2e time is 8,931.6 + P seconds\nbefore versus 5,421.6 + P seconds after, taking the unchanged post-e2e\nphase as P. Its duration remains unestablished: the host’s cold-read e2e\nfailure prevented a completed post-e2e phase; partial-input timings were\ncollected for both unchanged post-e2e targets.\n\nChanges avoid `src/`, `tests/e2e/`, Cargo manifests and lockfiles, and\nbudget files, keeping this work separate from the upcoming crate and\ntest split.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <19440155+nickderobertis@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b84dcd3794a65432ef993dc2867bd9b50e2a7530","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/trees/b84dcd3794a65432ef993dc2867bd9b50e2a7530"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/commits/0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq5XZQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARMAQACkl5ZtwOwEjrtJa2xMqhIMB\nib+X8CXoj2x09Oo2liZKSwTgnHZ5bIJGl9IAVl/0St99nfOEzehlxEYs6gOfsFbR\nsaWPp4MiDTb5hv7v20iGBWlS3o2lOirDQTojHeLN3/Vr1qGqOVJ77vWuZJu5MRdH\nQnFA7IF46Frw5h7xB4Xer4OIW4uULOFb0ZnD2JcKkFs0qTRLnvreKEyFwfTIKgys\nnunegHdlfxsgAVxUEWAPvZVAEX614vCPOBkdV7GOJTod2aIip1qCcR9p8T4+dK3s\nDiF6EE0jgrkS6C59X3P20CYM/DJixyd/sWGBRYqddrx6mdnwJRhJk7G8rjzE/12S\nf1M2RvbhDaIKqaIV7ef8Yvdrr+coK9b8fBtrm2bozgGRgwMQpzBoMeImWkiJ583y\n17AEJObgWhAkaBnH4XflHBgtUEVJh1dMbTStzvWbPd9R5WlfsmrcC44jkIWujB20\njn58sJfOcWaCASsejZ/K3cgZ6WsHfzRkkGjrBpHebbkdeLmJ0i32OdXOASWhExsi\nbhCxTL11qP6ehArFam8gsTKJeBkVTu+e+p2/VATOr6x5MZvVOZB48phdaOCct+sv\nZ3fn5He9Q9wyR4I9jKw9L0SB0ucjzNV/Jcxzld4CkPwmJw6xauRk4tp0N9pTkmDa\nmxmv0hpz6zrvWo1MDace\n=ZdnN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b84dcd3794a65432ef993dc2867bd9b50e2a7530\nparent 99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1793422928 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793422928 -0600\n\nperf: cut the onepipeline gate's work outside the e2e tier (#1320)\n\n## What\n\nSpeed up the non-e2e gate by reusing the debug build, compiling the\nstop-verdict release binary alongside other tasks, and running\nstaged-artifact corruption checks four at a time with faster fixture\ncompression. Preserve every existing test and assertion, with regression\ncoverage for build reuse, scheduling, artifact consumption, and build\nfailures.\n\n## Why\n\nBring pull-request test jobs toward the 30-minute goal and make local\ngates faster without cutting coverage. Linux’s non-e2e work alone\npreviously took 49.5 minutes, so skipping unaffected e2e suites cannot\nmeet that goal.\n\n## Additional info\n\nComparable-load host measurements show median pre-e2e gate time falling\nfrom 8,090 s to 4,580 s (43%). Total non-e2e time is 8,931.6 + P seconds\nbefore versus 5,421.6 + P seconds after, taking the unchanged post-e2e\nphase as P. Its duration remains unestablished: the host’s cold-read e2e\nfailure prevented a completed post-e2e phase; partial-input timings were\ncollected for both unchanged post-e2e targets.\n\nChanges avoid `src/`, `tests/e2e/`, Cargo manifests and lockfiles, and\nbudget files, keeping this work separate from the upcoming crate and\ntest split.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <19440155+nickderobertis@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-31T05:02:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commit/0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d/comments","author":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commit/99b620df27c00177d4d69e0c4765302bbc16a21a"}]},{"sha":"da460300fa11006304d74ef5c6d0f5763eeb2603","node_id":"C_kwDOTx8aUdoAKGRhNDYwMzAwZmExMTAwNjMwNGQ3NGVmNWM2ZDBmNTc2M2VlYjI2MDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick DeRobertis","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-31T08:28:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-31T08:28:14Z"},"message":"perf: cut onepipeline's per-test cost in the e2e suite and library (#1278)\n\n## What\n\nReduce e2e setup and process costs with shared builds and fixtures,\nbatched repository seeding, native cleanup, and faster debug startup.\nUnobserved attached launches exit without an unnecessary two-second\ndrain; maintenance reports reliably reach close-out, and large-root\ndiscovery reads launch records concurrently while preserving validation\nand order.\n\nThe existing crate and suite layout, per-case CLI coverage, scale\nassertions, and coverage threshold remain intact. Cached host fixtures\nreject malformed metadata, including duplicate live-run names.\n\n## Why\n\nWindows e2e tests averaged 21 seconds each, making the suite take over\ntwo hours and leaving the slowest platform to determine how long every\nchange waits. Making each test cheaper preserves coverage and frees\nshared job slots sooner.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe measured reductions do **not** bring any platform below 30 minutes.\nThe manager approved the projected overruns; shorter budget windows and\nreplacing per-case CLI calls with in-process calls remain outside this\nchange.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Performance evidence and remaining costs</summary>\n\nThese measurements precede the merge of main at `f5146966` and the\nsubsequent fixture-validation fix at `56259ab0`; they are not\nmeasurements of the final tree. Baseline is profile run F\n(`c49dda5e-20e7-45fe-b6e2-995cad542eec`, 1,912 records). The later full\nrecording is on `117e7352`, run `728f1477-5b41-4dca-b63b-19bea2d95958`,\nwith 1,924 tests: 1,922 passed, one failed on missing host I/O\naccounting, and one timed out during a cold test-double build. The\ntimed-out adoption test passed independently twice; the comparison\nsubstitutes its instrumented record from\n`75000004-f558-45a6-b4e7-31b2cfec86e0`.\n\n| Host Linux cost category, test-seconds | Baseline | `3de157d4` |\n`117e7352` |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Spawn | 21,300.6 | 15,107.6 | 13,337.3 |\n| Git | 1,097.6 | 753.1 | 897.5 |\n| Build | 6,542.3 | 12.0 | 150.7 |\n| Fixture | 51.5 | 20.7 | 29.4 |\n| Wait | 6,308.4 | 5,757.0 | 6,062.2 |\n| Filesystem | 334.0 | 168.7 | 244.2 |\n| Unattributed | 980.8 | 2,195.8 | 2,173.3 |\n| **Total** | **36,615.1** | **24,014.9** | **22,894.5** |\n\nProgram starts fell from 11,531 to 8,573 for `onepipeline`, 9,216 to\n7,225 for git, and 3,764 to 6 for Cargo. Node starts changed from 39 to\n68 and `ps` from 2,561 to 2,595. The later recording had higher host\nload: median load1 58.6 versus 45.6 at `3de157d4`. Its build category\nincludes a cold rebuild after changing dependency optimization.\n\nPaired runs provide separate evidence: 130 CLI-heavy tests all passed in\nevery pass, falling from 510.0 to 300.0 test-seconds (128.0 to 75.4\nseconds wall, about 41%). Schema-registry startup fell from 133–186 ms\nto 23–39 ms. Across 57 publication tests passing in both temporary\ncheckouts, paired totals improved about 20%; four additional\nold-checkout failures came from inherited discovery configuration and\npassed in the new checkout.\n\nThe projections apply the profile's platform/category ratios, schedule\nthe exclusive group first and ordinary tests across four Linux/Windows\nslots or three macOS slots, and use the spike's p90/median ratios. They\napply equally to the commonest one-project PR and a lockfile PR; no\nskipped suites, sharding, or crate split is credited.\n\n| Platform | Projected e2e test-seconds | E2e wall | E2e p90 | Job p90\nincluding other work | With carried proof work p90 | Unattributed\nsensitivity p90 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Linux | 8,687 | 2,686 s | 3,308 s | 3,762 s | 6,513 s | 6,810 s |\n| macOS | 11,357 | 4,316 s | 5,181 s | 6,537 s | 8,107 s | 8,657 s |\n| Windows | 38,467 | 11,527 s | 14,291 s | 15,775 s | 17,832 s | 19,299\ns |\n\nOther job work is the spike's 369 seconds for Linux (a lower bound),\n1,129 for macOS, and 1,197 for Windows. Platform-only tests use the\ncostliest test in their module as donor. Carried proof work is\nconditional on its placement in the later CI jobs. Linux's exclusive\nhost-sized tests explain why projected wall time did not fall with\naggregate test-seconds.\n\nCost-centre disposition:\n\n- **Spawn:** optimized debug schema/regex dependencies and removed the\nunobserved attachment drain tail. Per-case CLI calls remain. Most\nremaining publication git calls belong to `onevcs`; one four-node\nreadjust journey starts 4,034 git processes, so that work was drafted\nfor the sibling library.\n- **Test-side git:** repository seeding uses batched plumbing. Remaining\nstarts are distributed across real repository journeys.\n- **Build:** successful test-double builds are shared across test\nprocesses; failures remain retryable.\n- **Fixture:** host-sized fixtures are generated once and copied with\nlive-process identities rebound and journals independent. Scale\nassertions retain their scale.\n- **Wait:** existing pacing floors remain; deliberate quiet,\nrelease-poll, lease and takeover windows were not shortened. The channel\njourney ends its live listener with a reply instead of relying on a\none-second assertion window.\n- **Unattributed teardown:** cleanup calls the same stop API used by the\nCLI, with environment restoration; explicit stop journeys still drive\nthe binary. Skipping settled-run cleanup and replacing the `ps` reaper\nremain follow-ups.\n- **Filesystem and slow scale tests:** no further coverage-preserving\nreduction was identified. Publication chains retain their\ntransitive-restack assertions. Windows Dev Drive/Defender configuration\nremains a runner concern.\n\nThe full per-module comparison, platform ratios, projections, paired\nlogs and raw recording are retained under\n`/home/whoop/ai-orchestrator/runs/ci-time-budgets-wave1/scratch/857418-79`:\n`final-profile-117e7352/`, `pacing-profile-117e7352/`,\n`final-record-117e7352.{log,load}`, `compare-117e7352.mjs`,\n`project-finished.py`, `finished-comparison.json`,\n`finished-projections.json`, `previous-3de157d4-comparison.json`,\n`ab-*.log`, `pair-*.log`, `checks/`, and `checks2/`. Baseline raw\nrecords are no longer present; their retained aggregates are the\ncomparison source.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence provenance and current limitations</summary>\n\nThe [required llmlint\nfailure](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41174365927/job/124458737760)\nidentified a launch-record comment left above code that now only\ncollects paths. `fc8317f5` moves that explanation onto the reader it\ndescribes. `56259ab0` also rejects duplicate live-run names in cached\nfixture manifests, answering a subsequent boundary-validation finding.\nThe added refusal case failed with the validation removed and passed\nwith it restored.\n\nOn the final tree at `56259ab0`, judged diff lint exited successfully:\nhistory `20261031T061330Z-385f7` reports 17 passed, zero failed, 18\nskipped and four not relevant across 39 rules. The configured local\nharness-wrapper path was missing, so the command selected the installed\n`oneharness` executable through `LLMLINT_ONEHARNESS_BIN`; no lint\nconfiguration or wrapper file changed. Rust formatting and e2e Clippy\nchecks passed. The npm crate-split replay test passed 25/25. The\nhost-view module passed 11/12, including the fixture-validation\nregression.\n\nThe remaining host-view failure is\n`host_view::the_host_view_answers_a_host_sized_root_steady_cold_and_steady_again`.\nThis WSL host has neither `/proc/self/io` nor `/proc/thread-self/io`, so\nits cold-read accounting reports zero bytes. The assertion predates the\ntask base (`61194ef6`, #861) and remains unchanged. The required Linux\nCI check supplies its verdict; no local green gate is claimed.\n\nEarlier evidence remains explicitly historical:\n\n- Main at `e357c4f0` was merged through `f5146966`, resolving the\ninherited `crate-split-replay` failure. On that merged tree, the\naffected check run covered 17 projects; targets passed except the e2e\ntarget and four dependent targets that could not start. A separate e2e\nrun passed 1,959/1,959 in 3,802.591 seconds with the host-incompatible\ntest filtered out. That full run precedes the final fixture-validation\nchange and was not repeated afterward.\n- On `117e7352`, the new attachment-exit regression and related modules\npassed 181/181; before the fix, the new assertion observed a 2,069 ms\ndrain delay. The rest tier passed 1,317/1,317 after installing the\npinned tool, and contract/note/codex-server/stop-verdict passed 38/38.\nBudgets and crate documentation passed.\n- Coverage measured **96.00% lines** on the earlier recording and other\ntiers, after removing stale coverage binaries. It was not remeasured\nafter merging main. The final tree's coverage floor, budgets and\ndependent aggregate checks remain for CI.\n- `10ec7848` added the missing-fixture repair diagnostic and its refusal\ncase, plus explanatory test suppressions. Its host-view module passed\n11/12, with the same host-accounting failure; the changed unwatched\njourney passed. Format and relevant Clippy checks passed. Node\nformat/lint/syntax checks passed; release tests passed 58/58, workflow\ntests 63/63, and llmlint-diff tests passed. The then-failing npm replay\ntest was resolved by the merge.\n- Judged lint history `20261031T020305Z-34ba7` reported two findings,\nanswered by `10ec7848`. History `20261031T021304Z-a3029` then reported\n18 passed, zero failed, 18 skipped and three not relevant across 39\nrules. These earlier results are superseded for the final diff by\n`20261031T061330Z-385f7` above; the required hosted llmlint check\nremains the merge verdict.\n\nSuppression explanations retained in the diff cover the test-only Cargo\nrecorder in `crates/testfakes/Cargo.toml`, the maintenance journey's\nreal linked-sibling fixture and test-project boundary, and the unwatched\njourney's deliberately malformed/restored launch records. The latter\nstate cannot be produced by a normal verb; assertions still read the\nbinary's output. No suppression was widened.\n\nFollow-ups were drafted for `onevcs` publication git volume, lazy\nvalidator compilation in `onemessagebus`, and teardown/reaper costs.\nEvidence can be rendered with `onepipeline transcript\nci-time-budgets-wave1 onepipeline-test-cost-r4`; merged-tree logs are\nunder\n`/home/whoop/ai-orchestrator/runs/ci-time-budgets-wave1/scratch/857418-86`.\n\nThe existing draft is\n[#1278](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278).\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <19440155+nickderobertis@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"716e154f227311421b790956ccf167c57e16d5e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/trees/716e154f227311421b790956ccf167c57e16d5e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/commits/da460300fa11006304d74ef5c6d0f5763eeb2603","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq5aaeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8w8QAHOKK0+KB8Q7M6CGqm54GlYZ\nBvdntrMpLGJ3lZpbT8z2FxuolVEuoGDq4tGKkdBYl+Dsd024oEgUXbMsJCKyCjTH\ngSjeJDdpp3Rq4zjOXxuGb5nVRIcSGahJFCwAXo5xYEVOmtNjaUJ30NahjTRSwzrw\nDf4+AbjbIbHGzJ57NeYclvB3opZGddi8hI1NlJAHq1Vc5Rfx9M8zudaq5Tf5X0da\nCfN8SGToZwJTri6SvlB0qCfK8TDnVsAiJTgViyhQqP//LPOoVojR7strNPZOSRWY\nWhCJzpd/XBj5FsiW7SXruVpL7RXYL97McLV/9AW2zU3Pv01pHKPmIy+/mTPuJC76\nlpgovd8BnHls5MzBriJJSF9BfLvD/1pOyO5XCmbOPthnkxSa02A7lSQlR3gRGCvC\n0iFDoiBmpaNKq1uRj+4ZBoXMbqERLhmwIgOUrHrQsFQOLmDJBNh+J9XkI3c+gPhT\nvKBkl6y3LNugriscDuM8L5tFJ/sNaUrO2dBy6WHRxnTPhWpBg6BakuJEXR3IrDZC\ntVNenKWRnjKk/QJDEkbjpv5ck1SSM3Bum86xBJ7fWm5dwWqKXP0yoU5Xdq0xV+Qn\ngOBSbDs/PcB9j3Dl1UlXy4XcR93/oMN/6qHsHnoNc00/OABPJeFdDZRcbJJIshf6\njDDR+d12r/oEaIBHkoHR\n=CMB/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 716e154f227311421b790956ccf167c57e16d5e7\nparent 0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1793435294 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793435294 -0600\n\nperf: cut onepipeline's per-test cost in the e2e suite and library (#1278)\n\n## What\n\nReduce e2e setup and process costs with shared builds and fixtures,\nbatched repository seeding, native cleanup, and faster debug startup.\nUnobserved attached launches exit without an unnecessary two-second\ndrain; maintenance reports reliably reach close-out, and large-root\ndiscovery reads launch records concurrently while preserving validation\nand order.\n\nThe existing crate and suite layout, per-case CLI coverage, scale\nassertions, and coverage threshold remain intact. Cached host fixtures\nreject malformed metadata, including duplicate live-run names.\n\n## Why\n\nWindows e2e tests averaged 21 seconds each, making the suite take over\ntwo hours and leaving the slowest platform to determine how long every\nchange waits. Making each test cheaper preserves coverage and frees\nshared job slots sooner.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe measured reductions do **not** bring any platform below 30 minutes.\nThe manager approved the projected overruns; shorter budget windows and\nreplacing per-case CLI calls with in-process calls remain outside this\nchange.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Performance evidence and remaining costs</summary>\n\nThese measurements precede the merge of main at `f5146966` and the\nsubsequent fixture-validation fix at `56259ab0`; they are not\nmeasurements of the final tree. Baseline is profile run F\n(`c49dda5e-20e7-45fe-b6e2-995cad542eec`, 1,912 records). The later full\nrecording is on `117e7352`, run `728f1477-5b41-4dca-b63b-19bea2d95958`,\nwith 1,924 tests: 1,922 passed, one failed on missing host I/O\naccounting, and one timed out during a cold test-double build. The\ntimed-out adoption test passed independently twice; the comparison\nsubstitutes its instrumented record from\n`75000004-f558-45a6-b4e7-31b2cfec86e0`.\n\n| Host Linux cost category, test-seconds | Baseline | `3de157d4` |\n`117e7352` |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Spawn | 21,300.6 | 15,107.6 | 13,337.3 |\n| Git | 1,097.6 | 753.1 | 897.5 |\n| Build | 6,542.3 | 12.0 | 150.7 |\n| Fixture | 51.5 | 20.7 | 29.4 |\n| Wait | 6,308.4 | 5,757.0 | 6,062.2 |\n| Filesystem | 334.0 | 168.7 | 244.2 |\n| Unattributed | 980.8 | 2,195.8 | 2,173.3 |\n| **Total** | **36,615.1** | **24,014.9** | **22,894.5** |\n\nProgram starts fell from 11,531 to 8,573 for `onepipeline`, 9,216 to\n7,225 for git, and 3,764 to 6 for Cargo. Node starts changed from 39 to\n68 and `ps` from 2,561 to 2,595. The later recording had higher host\nload: median load1 58.6 versus 45.6 at `3de157d4`. Its build category\nincludes a cold rebuild after changing dependency optimization.\n\nPaired runs provide separate evidence: 130 CLI-heavy tests all passed in\nevery pass, falling from 510.0 to 300.0 test-seconds (128.0 to 75.4\nseconds wall, about 41%). Schema-registry startup fell from 133–186 ms\nto 23–39 ms. Across 57 publication tests passing in both temporary\ncheckouts, paired totals improved about 20%; four additional\nold-checkout failures came from inherited discovery configuration and\npassed in the new checkout.\n\nThe projections apply the profile's platform/category ratios, schedule\nthe exclusive group first and ordinary tests across four Linux/Windows\nslots or three macOS slots, and use the spike's p90/median ratios. They\napply equally to the commonest one-project PR and a lockfile PR; no\nskipped suites, sharding, or crate split is credited.\n\n| Platform | Projected e2e test-seconds | E2e wall | E2e p90 | Job p90\nincluding other work | With carried proof work p90 | Unattributed\nsensitivity p90 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Linux | 8,687 | 2,686 s | 3,308 s | 3,762 s | 6,513 s | 6,810 s |\n| macOS | 11,357 | 4,316 s | 5,181 s | 6,537 s | 8,107 s | 8,657 s |\n| Windows | 38,467 | 11,527 s | 14,291 s | 15,775 s | 17,832 s | 19,299\ns |\n\nOther job work is the spike's 369 seconds for Linux (a lower bound),\n1,129 for macOS, and 1,197 for Windows. Platform-only tests use the\ncostliest test in their module as donor. Carried proof work is\nconditional on its placement in the later CI jobs. Linux's exclusive\nhost-sized tests explain why projected wall time did not fall with\naggregate test-seconds.\n\nCost-centre disposition:\n\n- **Spawn:** optimized debug schema/regex dependencies and removed the\nunobserved attachment drain tail. Per-case CLI calls remain. Most\nremaining publication git calls belong to `onevcs`; one four-node\nreadjust journey starts 4,034 git processes, so that work was drafted\nfor the sibling library.\n- **Test-side git:** repository seeding uses batched plumbing. Remaining\nstarts are distributed across real repository journeys.\n- **Build:** successful test-double builds are shared across test\nprocesses; failures remain retryable.\n- **Fixture:** host-sized fixtures are generated once and copied with\nlive-process identities rebound and journals independent. Scale\nassertions retain their scale.\n- **Wait:** existing pacing floors remain; deliberate quiet,\nrelease-poll, lease and takeover windows were not shortened. The channel\njourney ends its live listener with a reply instead of relying on a\none-second assertion window.\n- **Unattributed teardown:** cleanup calls the same stop API used by the\nCLI, with environment restoration; explicit stop journeys still drive\nthe binary. Skipping settled-run cleanup and replacing the `ps` reaper\nremain follow-ups.\n- **Filesystem and slow scale tests:** no further coverage-preserving\nreduction was identified. Publication chains retain their\ntransitive-restack assertions. Windows Dev Drive/Defender configuration\nremains a runner concern.\n\nThe full per-module comparison, platform ratios, projections, paired\nlogs and raw recording are retained under\n`/home/whoop/ai-orchestrator/runs/ci-time-budgets-wave1/scratch/857418-79`:\n`final-profile-117e7352/`, `pacing-profile-117e7352/`,\n`final-record-117e7352.{log,load}`, `compare-117e7352.mjs`,\n`project-finished.py`, `finished-comparison.json`,\n`finished-projections.json`, `previous-3de157d4-comparison.json`,\n`ab-*.log`, `pair-*.log`, `checks/`, and `checks2/`. Baseline raw\nrecords are no longer present; their retained aggregates are the\ncomparison source.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence provenance and current limitations</summary>\n\nThe [required llmlint\nfailure](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41174365927/job/124458737760)\nidentified a launch-record comment left above code that now only\ncollects paths. `fc8317f5` moves that explanation onto the reader it\ndescribes. `56259ab0` also rejects duplicate live-run names in cached\nfixture manifests, answering a subsequent boundary-validation finding.\nThe added refusal case failed with the validation removed and passed\nwith it restored.\n\nOn the final tree at `56259ab0`, judged diff lint exited successfully:\nhistory `20261031T061330Z-385f7` reports 17 passed, zero failed, 18\nskipped and four not relevant across 39 rules. The configured local\nharness-wrapper path was missing, so the command selected the installed\n`oneharness` executable through `LLMLINT_ONEHARNESS_BIN`; no lint\nconfiguration or wrapper file changed. Rust formatting and e2e Clippy\nchecks passed. The npm crate-split replay test passed 25/25. The\nhost-view module passed 11/12, including the fixture-validation\nregression.\n\nThe remaining host-view failure is\n`host_view::the_host_view_answers_a_host_sized_root_steady_cold_and_steady_again`.\nThis WSL host has neither `/proc/self/io` nor `/proc/thread-self/io`, so\nits cold-read accounting reports zero bytes. The assertion predates the\ntask base (`61194ef6`, #861) and remains unchanged. The required Linux\nCI check supplies its verdict; no local green gate is claimed.\n\nEarlier evidence remains explicitly historical:\n\n- Main at `e357c4f0` was merged through `f5146966`, resolving the\ninherited `crate-split-replay` failure. On that merged tree, the\naffected check run covered 17 projects; targets passed except the e2e\ntarget and four dependent targets that could not start. A separate e2e\nrun passed 1,959/1,959 in 3,802.591 seconds with the host-incompatible\ntest filtered out. That full run precedes the final fixture-validation\nchange and was not repeated afterward.\n- On `117e7352`, the new attachment-exit regression and related modules\npassed 181/181; before the fix, the new assertion observed a 2,069 ms\ndrain delay. The rest tier passed 1,317/1,317 after installing the\npinned tool, and contract/note/codex-server/stop-verdict passed 38/38.\nBudgets and crate documentation passed.\n- Coverage measured **96.00% lines** on the earlier recording and other\ntiers, after removing stale coverage binaries. It was not remeasured\nafter merging main. The final tree's coverage floor, budgets and\ndependent aggregate checks remain for CI.\n- `10ec7848` added the missing-fixture repair diagnostic and its refusal\ncase, plus explanatory test suppressions. Its host-view module passed\n11/12, with the same host-accounting failure; the changed unwatched\njourney passed. Format and relevant Clippy checks passed. Node\nformat/lint/syntax checks passed; release tests passed 58/58, workflow\ntests 63/63, and llmlint-diff tests passed. The then-failing npm replay\ntest was resolved by the merge.\n- Judged lint history `20261031T020305Z-34ba7` reported two findings,\nanswered by `10ec7848`. History `20261031T021304Z-a3029` then reported\n18 passed, zero failed, 18 skipped and three not relevant across 39\nrules. These earlier results are superseded for the final diff by\n`20261031T061330Z-385f7` above; the required hosted llmlint check\nremains the merge verdict.\n\nSuppression explanations retained in the diff cover the test-only Cargo\nrecorder in `crates/testfakes/Cargo.toml`, the maintenance journey's\nreal linked-sibling fixture and test-project boundary, and the unwatched\njourney's deliberately malformed/restored launch records. The latter\nstate cannot be produced by a normal verb; assertions still read the\nbinary's output. No suppression was widened.\n\nFollow-ups were drafted for `onevcs` publication git volume, lazy\nvalidator compilation in `onemessagebus`, and teardown/reaper costs.\nEvidence can be rendered with `onepipeline transcript\nci-time-budgets-wave1 onepipeline-test-cost-r4`; merged-tree logs are\nunder\n`/home/whoop/ai-orchestrator/runs/ci-time-budgets-wave1/scratch/857418-86`.\n\nThe existing draft is\n[#1278](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278).\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <19440155+nickderobertis@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-31T08:28:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/da460300fa11006304d74ef5c6d0f5763eeb2603","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commit/da460300fa11006304d74ef5c6d0f5763eeb2603","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits/da460300fa11006304d74ef5c6d0f5763eeb2603/comments","author":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d","url":"https://api.github.co